{
  "info": {
    "name": "SC-403 - Caso Practico 2 - BiblioApp",
    "_postman_id": "sc403-caso2-biblioapp",
    "description": "Coleccion para probar la API REST de BiblioApp (Caso Practico 2).\n\nORDEN DE USO:\n1. 'Login BIBLIOTECARIO' -> guarda el JWT en la variable {{token}} automaticamente.\n2. Cualquier otro request usa ese token en el header Authorization.\n3. Para probar el 403, correr 'Login LECTOR' y despues los requests de la carpeta 'Pruebas de autorizacion'.\n\nVariables: base_url (http://localhost:8082) y token (se llena sola en el login).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8082",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Autenticacion (JWT)",
      "description": "POST /api/auth/login devuelve un JWT firmado con HS256, valido 1 hora.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login BIBLIOTECARIO (biblio/biblio123)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Credenciales del bibliotecario. El test script guarda el token en {{token}}.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"biblio\",\n  \"password\": \"biblio123\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Guarda el token en la variable de coleccion {{token}}",
                  "const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', data.token);",
                  "pm.test('200 y token presente', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(data.token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login LECTOR (lector/lector123)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
